Keep an error in any file operand in dc's exit status.
When standard input is a terminal, an error in a file operand does
not end dc: the rest of that file is skipped and the next file runs.
But zxc_vm_exec() stored the status of each file over that of the one
before, so the exit status reflected only the last file, and
"dc bad.dc good.dc" exited with status 0 after reporting the error.
Keep the error status once any file has failed. bc is unchanged, since
it reads standard input after its files, and that status still
decides.

---
 miscutils/bc.c |    5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/miscutils/bc.c
+++ b/miscutils/bc.c
@@ -7400,7 +7400,10 @@
 	s = BC_STATUS_SUCCESS;
 	fname = (void*)G.files.v;
 	for (i = 0; i < G.files.len; i++) {
-		s = zxc_vm_file(*fname++);
+		// An error in any file, not just the last, is the exit status
+		BcStatus st = zxc_vm_file(*fname++);
+		if (st)
+			s = st;
 		if (ENABLE_FEATURE_CLEAN_UP && !G_ttyin && s) {
 			// Debug config, non-interactive mode:
 			// return all the way back to main.
